# Sequential whole-proof completion v5

Preparation only. No native command or coordinator may run until the complete source manifest and prior-admission implementation receive independent review. All failed v2/v3/v4 sources, receipts, partials and the blocked v4 final-checker preparation remain unchanged.

Generation 1 completes eleven fresh mutation/rejection cases. After its suite and every registered native group are observed empty, generation 2 completes ten fresh cases. Generation 2 separately embeds the successful v4 cost rejection, whose original complete construction, fresh verifier, protected output and exact retirement are replayed by `prior_cases_v5.admit_v4_c2_cost`. The v4 enclosing suites keep their literal `input-changed` status and the v4 coordinator remains failed. The prior twelve rejections and two controls per generation are independently replayed by `prior_cases_v5.review`. No deleted old body is required or recreated.

There is at most one active suite and one mutation across both generations. The shared limits remain 26 GiB owned disk, 12 GiB sampled RSS and 8 GiB physical free floor. Helper limits remain 1800 seconds wall/CPU, 1 GiB sampled RSS and the exact per-generation proof-size allowance. Fresh verifier limits remain 7500 seconds wall/CPU, 6 GiB sampled RSS and 32 MiB output. The original outer schedule limit remains 86400 monotonic seconds.

Before each generation launch and each fresh mutation, capacity admission repeatedly measures the actual complete owned inventory and current physical free space. It reserves only the active proof plus 32 MiB mutation growth, 112 MiB output and two 256 MiB metadata buckets. Physical headroom is `max(growth + 8 GiB, active proof + 32 MiB + 10 GiB)`. The inventory includes every earlier retained scope, including all three v4 scopes and every earlier v5 generation. No projected future deletion or logical unlink receipt reduces this measurement.

Each capacity wait is bounded to 600 monotonic seconds, sampled every second, inside the unchanged outer deadline. It retains every refusal and the actual successful measurement in fresh bounded logs. Expiry fails the new scope without starting the waiting native command. This wait accounts for delayed physical reclamation; it never retries a native command or changes its deadline.

`admission-c1.json` and `admission-c2.json` are immutable and distinct. Each binds the admitted suite PID/birth, exact measured generation permit, source/plan and original outer deadline. The active-generation file is a restrictive switch bound to that immutable admission. Every construction and verification requires its exact generation/case permit. Preexec registration rechecks authorization while holding the accounting lock, and guard receipts retain both admission and capacity identities. Completed per-generation receipts precede the next launch.

The unchanged v4 ownership implementation is copied byte-for-byte. Cleanup retains per-record failures, handles every successfully started child, observes birth-aware group quiescence, and sweeps native registrations before and after suite shutdown under the original registration lock. All original/v2/v3/v4 coordinator and suite leases are held throughout v5. Only a completed current v5 mutation may be reclaimed; no historical deletion is authorized.

Tests use pure process mocks and tiny temporary receipts. They cover delayed free-space visibility, refusal/expiry, actual inventory remeasurement, unchanged extra headroom, outer deadline, immutable admissions, inactive-generation rejection, omitted per-case permits, no repeated C2 cost, one shared mutation, late registration, PID reuse/EPERM and all historical leases. First fixture failures remain in `runner-validation-1`; later validation receipts are distinct.
